BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-202316@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260923T170000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260923T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260923T183000
SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: Boston\, Our Global Home 
LOCATION:The Muse
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 24 spots lef
 t\nStatus: Waitlist Only\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/even
 ts/202316\n\n5:00PM Reception\, 5:30PM Discussion \nWhat makes Boston a t
 ruly global city? From the FIFA World Cup and America’s 250th anniversar
 y to the arrival of ships from around the world for Sail Boston\, the city
  continues to take center stage. Yet Boston’s international reach exten
 ds far beyond these marquee moments. Recently named the best U.S. city for
  foreign multinationals by The Financial Times and Nikkei\, Boston is h
 ome to more than 50 foreign and honorary consulates\, with one in four r
 esidents being born abroad. Across our universities\, hospitals\, busines
 ses\, cultural institutions\, and diverse communities\, Boston’s connect
 ions span the globe.\n\nFor this ’Quin Chat\, join James Reginald Colimo
 n\, Director of Global Affairs for the City of Boston\, and Mary Yntema\, 
 Executive Director of the Boston Committee on Foreign Relations and Past P
 resident & CEO of WorldBoston\, Inc.\, for a timely conversation exploring
  how Boston became the global hub it is today - and what that means for th
 e people who call it home.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved fo
 r members only. Complimentary light bites and refreshments will be served.
  We kindly ask that all cancellations be made at least 24 hours prior to t
 he start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/202316
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
