BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-203291@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260927T164500Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260927T164500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260927T193000
SUMMARY:Sunday Screening: "Pretty Dirty"
LOCATION:The Muse
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nStatus: Waitlist Only\nEvent U
 RL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/203291\n\n4:45PM Doors Open\, 
 5:00PM Screening\, 7:15PM Q&A\nGlamorous\, provocative\, and unapologetica
 lly unflinching\, Marilyn Minter has spent nearly five decades pushing the
  boundaries of contemporary art. In this Sunday Screening\, filmmaker Aman
 da Benchley turns the lens on the trailblazing feminist artist - moving b
 etween biography\, studio practice\, and cultural history - to trace Min
 ter’s rise through New York’s art world\, the controversies her work s
 parked within feminist discourse\, and the enduring influence of her lush\
 , subversive imagery. Fast-paced\, stylish\, and punctuated by notable 
 cameos\, the film offers an intimate portrait of an artistwho has contin
 ually challenged convention while embracing pleasure\, beauty\, and desire
  as forms of power.\n\nFollowing the screening\, members are invited to st
 ay for an intimate talkback with visionary filmmaker Amanda Benchley and M
 arilyn Minter herself. Together\, they will pull back the curtain on the
  making of the film\, Minter’s extraordinary career\, and the ideas and 
 experiences that have shaped both her art and the film.\n\n*This event is 
 complimentary and reserved for members only. Theatre fare and refreshments
  will be served. We kindly ask that all cancellations be made at least 24 
 hours prior to the start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/203291
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
