UID:quin-event-203633@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260930T183000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260930T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260930T200000
SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: How Hip-Hop Built an Empire
LOCATION:The Muse
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 70 spots left\nS
 tatus: futureSale\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/2036
 33\n\n6:30PM Reception\, 7:00PM Discussion\n\nWhat is it about hip-hop tha
 t has transformed generations of artists into some of the world’s most i
 nfluential entrepreneurs\, tastemakers\, and cultural forces? Join us for 
 a ’Quin Chat exploring the evolution of the hip-hop artist from performe
 r to mogul - and how a genre born from creative expression has become a po
 werful engine for business\, innovation\, and cultural influence. From fas
 hion and record labels to food and beverage\, technology\, media\, and bey
 ond\, the conversation will examine how artists have built expansive ecosy
 stems around their creativity while reshaping the industries they enter. 
 \n\nNeil Martinez Belkin\, New York Times bestselling author\, will be j
 oined in conversation by Boston native Dart Adams\, an acclaimed journalis
 t\, historian\, researcher\, lecturer\, and author. Together\, they will 
 explore the entrepreneurial mindset behind hip-hop’s most influential fi
 gures\, the relationship between cultural credibility and commercial succe
 ss\, and how the genre continues to redefine what it means to be an artist
 \, and a mogul\, today.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for m
 embers only. Complimentary light bites and refreshments will be served. We
  kindly ask that all cancellations be made at least 24 hours prior to the 
 start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/203633
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-203637@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261002T173000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261002T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261002T190000
SUMMARY:The Root of Wellbeing with Wildsmith Skin 
LOCATION:The Terrace
DESCRIPTION:Category: Health & Wellness\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 50 spot
 s left\nStatus: futureSale\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/ev
 ents/203637\n\n5:30PM Reception\, 6:00PM Discussion\n\nDiscover the root o
 f wellbeing with Wildsmith Skin and an intimate\, immersive evening explor
 ing the powerful role botanicals can play in how we sleep\, restore\, and 
 feel each day. Led by Haley Carr\, Vice President of Operations & Training
  at Wildsmith Skin\, the conversation will explore the foundations of well
 being and the importance of our circadian rhythm in supporting sleep quali
 ty\, gut and skin health\, relaxation\, and mental focus.\n\nWith more tha
 n 20 years of experience across the luxury spa\, wellness\, and hospitalit
 y industries\, Haley brings together expertise in aromatherapy\, skin heal
 th\, therapeutic touch\, and holistic wellbeing. Throughout the evening\, 
 members will discover the science and traditions behind Wildsmith’s bota
 nical ingredients while experiencing a selection of the brand’s products
  firsthand through their textures\, scents\, and formulations.\n\nThe expe
 rience extends beyond the conversation to dedicated one on one time with H
 aley\, offering each member personalized wellbeing guidance tailored to th
 eir lifestyle\, daily routine\, and individual needs. Leave with a deeper 
 understanding of your own wellness rituals—and simple\, achievable ways 
 to incorporate botanicals and thoughtful practices into everyday life.\n\n
 *This event is complimentary and reserved for members only. Complimentary 
 light bites and refreshments will be served. We kindly ask that all cancel
 lations be made at least 24 hours prior to the start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/203637
CATEGORIES:Health & Wellness
END:VEVENT
