SUMMARY:Author's Circle Book Club: "Safekeeping" by Claudia Hinz
LOCATION:The Muse
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 60 spots left\nS
 tatus: futureSale\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/2036
 29\n\nThis October\, settle into the season with Safekeeping by Claudia Hi
 nz\, a sweeping and deeply moving novel about family\, memory\, and the se
 crets we carry across generations. Set against the rugged beauty of Northe
 rn California\, the story follows the intertwined lives of three women as 
 long-held truths begin to surface\, revealing the complicated bonds betwee
 n mothers and daughters and the choices that shape a family over time.\n\n
 Atmospheric and richly layered\, Safekeeping explores belonging\, resilien
 ce\, and the ways our past continues to shape the present. With its evocat
 ive setting and intimate exploration of family relationships\, it is a fit
 ting fall read—and an ideal choice for readers drawn to thoughtful\, cha
 racter-driven stories that linger long after the final page.\n\nJoined by 
 author Claudia Hinz\, the evening will offer a closer look at the inspirat
 ion behind Safekeeping\, its characters\, and the themes woven throughout 
 the novel. Members will have the opportunity to hear directly from Hinz an
 d explore the story through an intimate conversation that brings the book 
 - and the world within it - to life.\n\n*This event is complimentary and r
 eserved for members only. Complimentary light bites and refreshments will 
 be served.We kindly ask that all cancellations be made at least 24 hours p
 rior to the start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/203629
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
